# REGION-1 evidence — audio region-boundary phase continuity (fable challenger, 2026-09-24)
# Fixture: fixtures/region1.txt — 60 s, 12x5 s events, 440->451 Hz drift (+1 Hz/event),
#   glide 0, amp 700, timbre 6. Renders: artifacts/WITHHELD-NOT-FOR-REVIEW/fable_chal/region1/
# Binaries: ../../crew_b/src/render_b_fix (B), ../../crew_servo/src/render_c_gated (gated-C),
#   ../../crew_servo/src/render_c_gfable (fable's gated C), stock/off controls, crew_d d1/d2/native.
#
# Method history: first metric (quadrature fit on 2048-sample windows each side of a
# boundary, compare phase) was CONFOUNDED by linear phase drift from a small systematic
# frequency offset (~4 mHz in gated-C: 1.6 rad drift over 58 s on the glide control).
# CITED metric (region_jump.py): jump(tb) = |wrap((phi(tb+5ms)-phi(tb-5ms)) - 2*pi*f_plan*10ms)|,
# immune to linear drift (a 4 mHz offset contributes ~0.0003 rad). Validated: synthetic
# continuous-phase step -> 0.0007 rad; synthetic reset -> 1.62 rad.
# Fable bar: mean over the 11 event boundaries < 0.1 rad.
#
# Renders (rc=0, wall clock this VM):
#   B:        19.94 s, 21,168,000 bytes (i64 LE mix, nev=12 regions=20 nsamp=2646000)
#   gated-C:  11.84 s, 5,292,000 bytes (i16 mix, 1 region — rest-gap defined, no latches)
#   gfable-C: 13.51 s, 5,292,000 bytes (1 region, servo never engaged: gs=0 all blocks)
#   stock-C:  15.81 s, 1 region
#   PAR-off:  12.87 s, 1 region
#   D1:       10.18 s | D2: 9.60 s | native(D): 12.47 s
#
# CITED RESULTS (drift-immune jump metric):
#   plan region1 (12x5 s events):
#     B:     11 event boundaries jump mean=0.0854 rad max=0.1345 -> PASS (<0.1)
#            19 internal 3 s region boundaries jump mean=0.0227 rad max=0.1054
#     gated: 11 event boundaries jump mean=0.1841 rad max=0.3888 -> FAIL
#     gfable:11 event boundaries jump mean=0.1841 rad max=0.3888 -> FAIL (identical to gated)
#     stock: 11 event boundaries jump mean=0.4321 rad max=1.1843 -> FAIL
#     off:   11 event boundaries jump mean=0.1841 rad max=0.3888 -> FAIL (identical to gated)
#   plan region1b (control: ONE 60 s event, glide 440->451 Hz, no event/region boundaries):
#     B:     5 s marks mean=0.0065 rad, 3 s marks mean=0.0081 rad (essentially perfect)
#     gated: 5 s marks mean=0.1674 rad, 3 s marks mean=0.1722 rad (interior estimator noise,
#            fine-grid scan shows no periodic jumps; spikes <=0.23 rad are harmonic-estimator
#            interference, not true phase steps)
#
# Signed jumps at the 11 event boundaries (12-event plan):
#   B:     -0.065 -0.064 -0.064 -0.066 -0.069 -0.075 -0.082 -0.093 -0.105 -0.121 -0.135
#   gated: -0.032 -0.018 -0.092 -0.098 -0.214 -0.176 -0.175 -0.251 -0.389 -0.317 -0.264
#   (off identical to gated; gfable identical to gated)
#
# Findings:
# 1. B PASSES the bar (0.0854 < 0.1); every C-family variant FAILS (0.184-0.432).
#    Fable's REGION-1 rationale is INVERTED by the data: B is ~2x more phase-continuous
#    than gated-C here, not the reverse.
# 2. Both contenders show SYSTEMATIC (not noisy) negative phase steps at event starts;
#    B's legato carry step (-0.065..-0.135) is ~2-3x smaller than the C family's
#    event-rendering step (-0.03..-0.39, growing with frequency).
# 3. The C-family step is NOT the servo: gated==off==gfable to 4 decimals, and the
#    servo logs show zero engagements (gs=0) on this clean drift. It is the C/PAR
#    event-rendering path's event-start phase behavior.
# 4. B's actual regions are 3 s (20 regions), not fable's assumed 5 s; its 3 s
#    reseed is phase-consistent (0.0227 rad). B's single-event glide control is
#    0.0065-0.008 rad.
# 5. Incidental: gated-C carries a ~4 mHz systematic frequency offset (1.6 rad phase
#    drift over 58 s on the glide control), consistent with its frozen-battery +0.1c
#    figure; harmless for the jump metric.
# 6. Latency (same renders, wall clock): B 19.94 s (3x RT, not RT-capable);
#    gated 11.84 s, gfable 13.51 s, stock 15.81 s, off 12.87 s, D1 10.18 s,
#    D2 9.60 s, native(D) 12.47 s (all RT-capable except B and stock-C).
